      {
        "description": "Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (UAV) images (Orthomosaic Image 3 of 3) collected for high resolution flood mapping\nin Karonga, Malawi. In the absence of housing stock data, remote sensed images \n(such as UAV imagery) are useful for infering building typologies and their \nvulnerability to flooding hazards. These processed UAV images were used for \ndetection and classification of buildings according to the materials used. The \nbuildings captured by the UAV images have two rooftypes: permanent (iron sheet) \nroofs and traditional (thatch) roofs.   ",
        "label": "mwakaboko2_ortho_corrected_big.tif",
